\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {15.1.1}{\ignorespaces The two passes on $T$ for CF~1187E. Green (top-right of each node) is $\mathit  {down}[v]=\size  (v)$ from the post-order pass; red below is $\mathit  {dp}[v]=F(v)=\Phi (\mathit  {down}[v],\mathit  {up}[v])$, the sum of subtree sizes when the tree is rooted at $v$, from the pre-order pass via the closed edge-transfer $F(c)=F(v)+n-2\size  (c)$. The maximum, $F(10)=48$, is CF~1187E's answer on $T$ -- reproduced as Example~\ref {ex:c20-twodfs-run}.}}{909}{figure.caption.155}\protected@file@percent }
